# Optional: raises the GitHub REST API rate limit from 60 requests/hour
# (unauthenticated) to 5000/hour, which matters if this site gets visits
# from a shared IP within the same hour.
#
# This value is bundled into the client-side JS at build time — anyone can
# read it from the browser's devtools/Network tab. Only use a fine-grained
# GitHub token scoped to "Public Repositories (read-only)" with no other
# access. Never use a classic PAT or one with write/private-repo scopes here.
#
# Create one at: https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the value:
VITE_GITHUB_TOKEN=
